{
  "date": "2026-10-23",
  "decision": "Superseded 2026-10-24: adopt detent::flat_map for the four model tables (see model-container-three-way-20261024.json). This record keeps the std::map step's evidence against btree 25f9494.",
  "application_base": "80d4071 (btree arm: FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_CPP_BTREE at 25f9494); std::map arm: this branch",
  "btree_revisions": {
    "production_pin": "cbc35762bc4a98ad91361be29d05f0ae715a1339",
    "ownership_qualified_head": "25f9494b64c02a63827e7294cb25a79762b7544f"
  },
  "actual_type_counterexamples": {
    "platform": "Linux x86_64, g++ 11.2.0 -std=c++20 -O1, ASan+UBSan, global operator new refusing the Nth allocation",
    "probe": "benchmarks/btree-repair/actual_type_sweep.cc (args: knobs|patch|group|cli, insert|erase|copy, short|long, max_n)",
    "findings": [
      "Relocation inside full or rebalanced nodes move-constructs pair<const string, V>; the const key is copied, so names longer than the small-string buffer allocate during relocation. A refused allocation there corrupts the table: lost or misordered entries, leaked allocations, and on erase an ASan double-free.",
      "25f9494 insert, long names: Snapshot::knobs and BoolDef::overrides violate contents/leak invariants (41 and 132 violations at max_n 40). Short names (<=15 bytes) never allocate during relocation and pass.",
      "25f9494 erase, long names: all four tables fail (erase refuses an allocation mid-rebalance after removing the entry; ASan double-free). std::map erase never allocates (0 refusals in 480 attempts).",
      "cbc3576 pin additionally publishes a wrong size after a refused nonfull insert (size N+1 != N, 118 to 174 violations per shape at max_n 12), the defect fixed later by bb2ad1d.",
      "patch/cli insert with long names and cli insert with short names did not finish inside the 80 s probe limit at max_n 40; they are not counted as pass or fail.",
      "const_cast in params::swap writes through const keys (language-level UB); no miscompile was demonstrated, and std::map removes the construct.",
      "parse_source_snapshot on a 40-knob snapshot with maximum-length names leaks when allocation 98 is refused (25f9494); std::map balances at every position.",
      "With maximum-length names, positional erase allocates on 25f9494: 52,007 allocations to prune half of a 100K snapshot and about 509 per 256-override drain, inside Detent's noexcept disposal paths, where a refusal terminates. std::map allocates zero.",
      "History: the sweep fails on every revision (35ac0ec 2019 import, 3e9f417, dd984d9, 25f9494); no earlier revision is a safe rollback point."
    ],
    "control": "std::map arm of the same probe: 0 violations for insert, erase and copy, short and long names."
  },
  "permanent_regression_test": {
    "source": "tests/detent/test_model_alloc_failure.cc",
    "scope": "all four model fields, insert/erase/copy, n=0..24, ordered and shuffled, four positions, short and 200/128-byte names, every refusal position; copy assignment checks the basic guarantee; lifecycle legs refuse each allocation of parse, copy, patch parse/apply, diff, compose and serialize",
    "btree_25f9494": "aborts: FAILED content at op=insert n=4 budget=12 long_names=1 (macOS arm64, Apple clang 17); n=3 on Linux g++ 11 (earlier revision of the test, smaller libstdc++ SSO)",
    "std_map": "PASS, 11 s on Linux with unsuppressed LeakSanitizer (two runs); passes in the full local suite"
  },
  "consumer_qualification": {
    "platform": "macOS arm64, Apple clang 17, Release, DETENT_BUILD_AUTHORITY=ON, benchmarks off",
    "result": "clean build with no cpp_btree fetch; ctest 208/208 passed (includes the new test)"
  },
  "compatibility": "Four public C++ field types change from btree::map to std::map: layouts (on macOS arm64: Snapshot 72 to 88 bytes, BoolDef 24 to 40 bytes), iterator types and size_type change. Rebuild every C++ consumer together. Serialized bytes, ordering, duplicate rejection and CLI behavior are unchanged by construction (std::less<>, same call sites).",
  "remaining": [
    "std::map costs 7.5% to 57% more total lifecycle CPU and 11% to 46% more live heap than btree 25f9494; a flat sorted map and a repaired btree with move relocation are being evaluated against it.",
    "Hash index (28.8 MB / 90.4 MB retained, 44-60% faster broad hits) is not selected: no adversarial-key policy and the sorted-publication cost is uncharged.",
    "Incremental cleanup: positional std::map erase is amortized constant; maximum cleanup-turn latency at the supported override limit and allocation-denied authority cleanup are not yet measured.",
    "Larger-system qualification (1.3M primary capacity tier, authority persistent-map and resource-task coordination) is outside this change.",
    "Upstream btree keeps its open const-key relocation defect; document it there rather than repairing it."
  ],
